          "answer": "Please contact a clinician promptly about this, today if you can. The search tool rated this as routine, but that rating only means its fixed list of warning patterns did not match. It is not a clearance. The guidance I retrieved does not cover calf pain and swelling after surgery, so I cannot tell you from these sources how much risk it carries.\n\n**Seek emergency care right away** (call your local emergency number) if you develop chest pain, sudden shortness of breath, coughing up blood, fainting, or a racing heartbeat. Those can be signs of a serious complication, and they need immediate attention.\n\nThe sources I searched were the osteoarthritis management guideline, the iron-deficiency anemia reference, the hypothyroidism reference, the osteoarthritis reference, and the lipid screening and statin guideline. None of them discuss clots or swelling after joint replacement. Your surgical team or your clinician can assess the leg and explain the risk for your situation. Tell them about the calf pain and swelling and the date of your surgery.\n\nNot medical advice. This is an educational software project. It does not diagnose or treat, and it must not be used for real medical decisions.",
